1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,891
The paper says 175.

2
00:00:02,941 --> 00:00:06,421
The official capture typed 75.

3
00:00:06,471 --> 00:00:09,950
The certified count says 175.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,950
Two Hands checks every number typed from paper, against the paper.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,950
On AMD, 310 forms audited so far.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,274
Pick any polling station. 169,000 of them.

7
00:00:24,324 --> 00:00:31,301
This one we have read: the page and its receipts, at once.

8
00:00:31,351 --> 00:00:34,004
This one, not yet.

9
00:00:34,054 --> 00:00:39,950
One click, and the reader on AMD takes it next.

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,807
How does it work? Two hands.

11
00:00:42,857 --> 00:00:48,521
The model on AMD reads every number twice: the digits, and the words.

12
00:00:48,571 --> 00:00:51,787
Then the gate: the form's own arithmetic.

13
00:00:51,837 --> 00:00:55,460
If it all adds up, nobody types anything.

14
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:59,950
If not, a person sees the rest, with the photo.

15
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,768
Measured, not promised.

16
00:01:01,818 --> 00:01:05,859
300 random forms, chosen before any model read.

17
00:01:05,909 --> 00:01:10,859
52 fields where the capture does not match the paper.

18
00:01:10,909 --> 00:01:15,405
Then we tested the fix on 100 new forms.

19
00:01:15,455 --> 00:01:18,586
Zero wrong, in 484 accepted fields.

20
00:01:18,636 --> 00:01:24,950
That is not proof of zero. It means: fewer than 1 in 100.

21
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,354
This is the product.

22
00:01:27,404 --> 00:01:32,162
An auditor brings the typed data and the scans.

23
00:01:32,212 --> 00:01:36,488
Here, the sample: 6,000 fields, checked in seconds.

24
00:01:36,538 --> 00:01:38,892
267 disputes, strongest first.

25
00:01:38,942 --> 00:01:42,738
Each has its photo and a receipt.

26
00:01:42,788 --> 00:01:46,104
One fingerprint seals the whole report.

27
00:01:46,154 --> 00:01:49,950
Change one number, and the check fails.

28
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,807
Now a live read.

29
00:01:52,857 --> 00:01:58,521
One request to Gemma, on the AMD Token Factory.

30
00:01:58,571 --> 00:02:04,236
We cut the wait. The timer stays on screen.

31
00:02:04,286 --> 00:02:07,093
It took 90 seconds.

32
00:02:07,143 --> 00:02:09,950
Every check holds: accepted.

33
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,582
Arithmetic has no language.

34
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:19,424
I filled this practice sheet by hand, in Czech and in English.

35
00:02:19,474 --> 00:02:25,739
The model reads my words and my digits. The sums decide.

36
00:02:25,789 --> 00:02:29,950
This is a demonstration, not a measurement.

37
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,450
Each strong finding becomes a case in Evolus.

38
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,450
This is our workspace, py_tr.

39
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:43,450
The agent runs on Gemma, on AMD, and drafts the finding.

40
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:47,950
A script, not the model, scores the evidence.

41
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,950
The auditor decides.

42
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,362
Who pays?

43
00:02:51,412 --> 00:02:56,068
The problem, in three lines from INE's own files.

44
00:02:56,118 --> 00:03:02,185
One: on 6.5% of stations, two official records of one paper disagree.

45
00:03:02,235 --> 00:03:07,832
Two: almost one form in five fails its own row sum.

46
00:03:07,882 --> 00:03:13,009
Three: the audit checks the software, not the typed numbers.

47
00:03:13,059 --> 00:03:18,656
INE tried to buy a machine first capture: MXN 9.5 million, an 80% bar.

48
00:03:18,706 --> 00:03:25,715
On that metric, as we read it, computed after the fact, we reach 83.5%.

49
00:03:25,765 --> 00:03:29,950
Auditors and PREP operators buy the check, at $1 per form.

50
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,610
Where does it fail?

51
00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:38,993
Unused ballots sit in no sum, so arithmetic cannot check them.

52
00:03:39,043 --> 00:03:42,184
Once, the model read 3,114.

53
00:03:42,234 --> 00:03:46,439
The paper says 314. One digit added.

54
00:03:46,489 --> 00:03:50,163
The first gate would accept it.

55
00:03:50,213 --> 00:03:54,950
Gate version two sent it to a person.

56
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,950
Two Hands.

57
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:02,283
Receipts for every number keyed from paper.

58
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:04,950
Running on AMD.
